1
00:00:00,05 --> 00:00:01,08
- [Instructor] When your app starts to grow,

2
00:00:01,08 --> 00:00:04,08
state management needs to be handled very effectively.

3
00:00:04,08 --> 00:00:06,06
Now, we want to focus on making the code

4
00:00:06,06 --> 00:00:08,08
more flexible and more maintainable,

5
00:00:08,08 --> 00:00:12,04
with the help of another hook: useReducer.

6
00:00:12,04 --> 00:00:14,07
useReducer is an alternative to useState

7
00:00:14,07 --> 00:00:17,05
that provides a more powerful and a more flexible way

8
00:00:17,05 --> 00:00:20,00
of managing the state in your components.

9
00:00:20,00 --> 00:00:23,03
It is especially useful for handling complex state logic

10
00:00:23,03 --> 00:00:26,01
as it allows to separate the state management logic

11
00:00:26,01 --> 00:00:27,04
from your components,

12
00:00:27,04 --> 00:00:30,04
making the code easier to understand, easier to maintain,

13
00:00:30,04 --> 00:00:31,09
and to test.

14
00:00:31,09 --> 00:00:34,05
And so, useReducer accept a reducer function

15
00:00:34,05 --> 00:00:36,09
and one initialState as parameters.

16
00:00:36,09 --> 00:00:38,04
Then, it returns an array

17
00:00:38,04 --> 00:00:40,09
with the current states and a dispatch method.

18
00:00:40,09 --> 00:00:43,08
So, let's see one example with useReducer.

19
00:00:43,08 --> 00:00:46,02
Until now, we have created and kept the state

20
00:00:46,02 --> 00:00:49,01
at the top level of the root components app.

21
00:00:49,01 --> 00:00:50,07
Instead, we would like to manage the state

22
00:00:50,07 --> 00:00:52,03
in a separate location,

23
00:00:52,03 --> 00:00:54,07
so let's do that with useReducer.

24
00:00:54,07 --> 00:00:57,01
We're going to replace all the state variables

25
00:00:57,01 --> 00:00:59,00
with useReducer.

26
00:00:59,00 --> 00:01:02,03
So, we're going to start by importing useReducer.

27
00:01:02,03 --> 00:01:04,08
You're going to add it through the scope right here

28
00:01:04,08 --> 00:01:06,04
of your app.gs.

29
00:01:06,04 --> 00:01:09,03
Let's go back to the root components,

30
00:01:09,03 --> 00:01:10,06
and right here, at the top level,

31
00:01:10,06 --> 00:01:12,06
you're going to call useReducer.

32
00:01:12,06 --> 00:01:14,05
It's going to return an array.

33
00:01:14,05 --> 00:01:17,07
And as parameters, you're going to have one reducer function.

34
00:01:17,07 --> 00:01:19,02
So, for now, it's not existing,

35
00:01:19,02 --> 00:01:21,07
so we're going to replace with an anonymous function,

36
00:01:21,07 --> 00:01:25,04
and one empty object as initialState.

37
00:01:25,04 --> 00:01:27,06
Then, it's going to return a state objects

38
00:01:27,06 --> 00:01:30,04
and a dispatch method.

39
00:01:30,04 --> 00:01:32,07
So next, we want to remove all the state variables

40
00:01:32,07 --> 00:01:34,04
that we have created with useState,

41
00:01:34,04 --> 00:01:36,08
so let's do that like this.

42
00:01:36,08 --> 00:01:38,08
But stop. Not just yet.

43
00:01:38,08 --> 00:01:40,06
First, you want to refactor the app

44
00:01:40,06 --> 00:01:43,04
and move all the logic in a reducer function.

45
00:01:43,04 --> 00:01:45,04
So, let's go back.

46
00:01:45,04 --> 00:01:50,04
We're going to first create a new function, reducer.

47
00:01:50,04 --> 00:01:52,09
So, we're just going to leave it as is for now.

48
00:01:52,09 --> 00:01:56,02
And also, we're going to create one initialState,

49
00:01:56,02 --> 00:01:59,07
an empty object that's going to hold the initialState.

50
00:01:59,07 --> 00:02:02,06
So, we're going to replace here with initialState

51
00:02:02,06 --> 00:02:07,02
and reducer for the function reducer.

52
00:02:07,02 --> 00:02:09,03
And so, the role of the function reducer

53
00:02:09,03 --> 00:02:11,04
will be to return a new state,

54
00:02:11,04 --> 00:02:13,06
and after that, all the data will be handled

55
00:02:13,06 --> 00:02:16,07
through the useReducer only.

56
00:02:16,07 --> 00:02:19,02
And so, the component will be able to read the state,

57
00:02:19,02 --> 00:02:20,05
the data,

58
00:02:20,05 --> 00:02:24,05
by reading from the state object like so.

59
00:02:24,05 --> 00:02:27,00
And so, useReducer is a preferred solution

60
00:02:27,00 --> 00:02:29,06
when the business logic of your app is starting to grow

61
00:02:29,06 --> 00:02:31,04
and become more complex.

62
00:02:31,04 --> 00:02:34,08
The goals are to separate the logic from the presentation,

63
00:02:34,08 --> 00:02:36,03
and move all the business logic

64
00:02:36,03 --> 00:02:38,08
in a separate function called reducer

65
00:02:38,08 --> 00:02:41,04
that we are yet to complete and to implement,

66
00:02:41,04 --> 00:02:43,00
and this is what we're doing next.

